        <briefdescription>
<para>Deprecated wrapping of a floating-point value with an explicit comparison tolerance. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The floating-point literals (<computeroutput>1.5_d</computeroutput>) and wrappers (<computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated-literals_1ga9608f4a6f0a61bc159a66a46fb8cd630" kindref="member">to_d</ref>{ 1.5 }</computeroutput>) compare with a tolerance derived from the number of decimals written (0.1 for <computeroutput>1.5</computeroutput>). <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated-logical-functions_1gafe47800a219b00fcccf0a1dc596dbe20" kindref="member">approx()</ref></computeroutput> makes the tolerance explicit, independent of how the value is written. All six comparisons apply it: values whose difference is less than the tolerance are equal, and neither less nor greater. If both operands have a tolerance, the smaller one is used.</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="normal">t.expect<sp/>(mt::eq<sp/>(compute_float<sp/>(),<sp/>mt::approx<sp/>(42.0f,<sp/>0.001f)));</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>For a single comparison, also of integers, the <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated-logical-functions_1gafe47800a219b00fcccf0a1dc596dbe20" kindref="member">approx</ref> (lhs, rhs, epsilon)</computeroutput> function comparator may be used instead.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The floating-point type of the value.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>value</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The expected value. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>epsilon</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The tolerance, converted to <computeroutput>T</computeroutput>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>A <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1value" kindref="compound">detail::value</ref>&lt;T&gt;</computeroutput> wrapper, recognised by the comparators and the operators.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Deprecated</title><para>Use the function comparator <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated-logical-functions_1gafe47800a219b00fcccf0a1dc596dbe20" kindref="member">approx</ref> (lhs, rhs, epsilon)</computeroutput> instead (since 6.0.0).</para>
